Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||05-10-2000||02:33 AM||||I was looking at V8 Archie's site last night, and I noticed he offers a brake kit..<P><I><B>"These products provide the Fiero with the handling and stopping power it deserves. All products have been designed to be "bolt-in" to the maximum extent possible. Two brake packages are available, both of which retain the Fiero bolt patterns, use vented rotors, provide for use of the stock hand brake cable and use readily available GM calipers."</I></B><P>Anyone know any details on this, price, what calipers it uses.. etc?<P>thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||05-10-2000||09:57 AM||||One half is from a camero the other is from a cadillac. I think its cadillac front and camero rear but I am not sure. Just E-mail Archie and ask him. Note the upgrade kit uses bigger vented rotors so the smallest wheel size you can use is a 16" rim. A 15" or less will not fit.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-10-2000).]||||reg||1
